  {
   "id": 519527,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "John will either lease or buy a car. The total cost to purchase the car is $35,830, and he would finance the car for 5 years at 2.99%. If he leases, he would pay $3,287.50 for the lease, and then his payments would be based on a price of $32,750, a residual price of $20,305, 36 months, with a money factor of 0.00001725. Compare the payments to purchase the car to the payments of the lease plus the lease cost divided by 36.",
